# CODEOWNERS — INV-T-2849 (T5), API-01 / FR-AH.13, the OW1 ownership decision
#
# "Only the owning service's team may change its directory" (API-01). No
# per-service GitLab group exists yet — every repository in `invoice/` is
# still built by the coding agents under one identity (AGT-20), not a
# differentiated human team per service (design-only phase). Until the owner
# creates one group per service, every directory defaults to the same
# reviewing identity that already gates every other merge in this project
# (AGT-20, CS-47) — a uniform rule first, tightened per directory once real
# teams exist (AGT-50), never the reverse.
#
# When a service gets its own ownership group, change only that line, here —
# CODEOWNERS itself is this task's declared scope; the groups it will
# eventually name are not.

/access/           @inv-reviewer
/aggregation/      @inv-reviewer
/canonical/        @inv-reviewer
/console-bff/      @inv-reviewer
/control-plane/    @inv-reviewer
/evidence/         @inv-reviewer
/ingestion/        @inv-reviewer
/masterdata/       @inv-reviewer
/notification/     @inv-reviewer
/payload/          @inv-reviewer
/reconciliation/   @inv-reviewer
/rules/            @inv-reviewer
/submission/       @inv-reviewer
/tenancy/          @inv-reviewer
/transport/        @inv-reviewer

# Shared components every directory above references by $ref (API-40, API-20) —
# owned by whoever owns the `service-runtime` L1 module (STK-60).
/service-runtime/  @inv-reviewer

# CI, lint and packaging plumbing for this repository (declared scope of
# INV-T-2849 itself) — reviewed the same way as any other platform-build-style
# change (CS-50's "own merge request" spirit: a build-configuration change here
# is visible, not silently bundled into a schema change).
/spectral/         @inv-reviewer
/.gitlab-ci.yml    @inv-reviewer
/build.gradle.kts  @inv-reviewer
/CODEOWNERS        @inv-reviewer
